{"id":"atlas-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3600,"height":200,"text":"**Services hub / NOS · 1.43-B**\n\n29 system members · 21 one-hop ghost neighbours · 61 canonical edges\nEvery incoming and outgoing edge of a member is shown, including parallel edges. Ghost cards retain status text and gap badges; grey borders mark neighbours unless a high/critical gap requires red. Arrows retain source direction; MISSING means an absent connection, not working data flow.\nCyan data · orange control · green persist · purple schedule · yellow UI · red event.\n[[NOS System Map.canvas|Return to overview]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"ext-ntp","type":"text","x":4836,"y":396,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**SNTP time server**\nInternet time source. Once Wi-Fi is up the…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Re-synced about hourly while Wi-Fi is connected.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"hw-pcf85063-rtc","type":"text","x":4836,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**PCF85063 RTC (0x51)**\nBattery-backed calendar chip on shared I2C.…\n\nruns: Hardware. Read once at boot; written when board_clock_changed is set.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|6 gaps]]\n[[Followup 1 - Time source, RTC trust and midnight rollover end to end|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
